pare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also strong: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart scheduling and connection loss, a changed boot identity, and recovered service, process identity, account, runlevel, binary integrity, OS, and kernel. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently match the executor's boot IDs.","limitations":["OpenRC failed-service enumeration was unavailable because the lifecycle probe only checks systemd; service health was nevertheless directly verified through OpenRC.","The worker has no identified persistent application data or cluster state, so those restart-protocol dimensions were not applicable beyond artifact integrity and single-node service recovery."]}
